  "selection_notes": {
    "slide_03_background_estimation_and_foreground_segmentation": "Final background curve: segmentation_slides_20261028-150504 (publication-style revision). Steps 2-4 and output: segmentation_slides_20261028-115531. Data include the pixel brightness series, original frame, binary mask and intermediate arrays. The curve shows the single-video percentile stage, before combining backgrounds.",
    "slide_04_multi_object_tracking": "Final figures: tracking_slides_20261028-122312. Data include the overlap matrix, measured shifts and trajectory excerpt.",
    "slide_06_motion_shape_and_collective_analysis": "Steps 1-3: analysis_slides_20261028-141412. Step 1 is the full-field animation without red cut circles, with PZT timeline at upper right and segment count at upper left. Step 4: analysis_slides_20261028-143326, the final white canvas/plot revision with a translucent legend. Output validation: 05_raw_video_validation from analysis_slides_20261028-134345, which was not superseded. Frame mappings and analysis tables are in data/. The 0.32 px value is a median difference between centroid and template displacements, not absolute tracking accuracy.",
    "slide_08_stimulus_response_analysis": "Final assets: stimulus_response_slides_20261028-144935. The second-switch figure uses 11/18; the original numerator 12 includes an object outside the resting population. Both records are preserved. Command-reference times are not calibrated ultrasound onset times. See provenance/original_notes.md for limitations.",
    "baseline_comparison": "Final assets: baseline_animations_20261028-154358. Each topic contains one baseline and one our-method movie. Baseline panels use thresholds 100 and 130; tracking displays independent single-target runs. All 20 baseline runs are included in data/baseline_runs/. Only accepted ours_fixed_background results are copied to data/our_method/. The diagnostic background-rebuild run is excluded. The baseline has no merger, separation or exit classifier; the event movie shows its actual behavior in the same scenes."
  },
